From 2dcce7b40973e0c34cecaf6c9e7a9dfbdd0060d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: steamac <steamac@local>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 09:30:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] kk: bound the indirect-deref branch tree and spill large
 arrays

nir_lower_indirect_derefs_to_if_else_trees lowered every indirect array
access into a full if-else tree with no size bound (UINT32_MAX), i.e. one
branch per array element.  Metal's MSL front end is super-linear in branch
count: measured on an M2, a balanced 8k-leaf tree costs ~9 s and a 30k-leaf
one ~44 s in MTLCompilerService, against ~7 ms for the same 80k accesses
through a dynamically indexed "thread" array.  Titles that generate shaders
per light / per morph (VRChat's world and mirror warming) hit this on the
presenting thread, which is the multi-second menu-open and fast-turn
freeze; the cost is repeated per pipeline because the MSL only reaches
Metal's own cache on an identical source string.

Bound the tree at a small leaf count (Apple's AGX uses 16) and spill the
larger function-temp arrays to scratch first, at a 64 B threshold, so their
dynamic index lowers to a flat scratch access instead of the tree.  Arrays
at or under the thresholds keep the direct/ tree form; arrays over them
become scratch loads/stores, which is the same dynamic index MSL already
receives through the existing scratch path (nir_to_msl.c emits
"thread uchar scratch[N]").  Cost is zero when unused: a shader with no
indirect arrays runs one extra pass that finds nothing to spill.

The nearby nir_lower_vars_to_scratch(32) only spilled arrays past 32 B (a
handful of elements), too low to keep the big generated arrays out of the
tree; the bound is what caps the tree itself.  MSL crashes on the 256-leaf
dEQP-VK.graphicsfuzz.stable-binarysearch-tree case noted in the file, so a
lower bound is strictly the smaller tree and the safe direction.

The bound applies to function_temp only. shader_in/out keep the full,
unbounded tree in a call of their own: nir_to_msl emits those as
load_input/store_output and reads the offset with nir_src_as_uint, so an
indirect index into them cannot be expressed, and KosmicKrisp never calls
nir_lower_io_indirect_loads. A single call with the bound would have left
a dynamically indexed input/output array longer than 16 elements (geometry
or tessellation per-vertex arrays, large varying arrays) unlowered.

Upstream state: KosmicKrisp at MESA_COMMIT passes UINT32_MAX here; this is
genuinely absent behaviour, not a stock option.
---
 src/kosmickrisp/compiler/nir_to_msl.c | 37 +++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 35 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/kosmickrisp/compiler/nir_to_msl.c b/src/kosmickrisp/compiler/nir_to_msl.c
index 875fdf9..dfa7834 100644
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/compiler/nir_to_msl.c
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/compiler/nir_to_msl.c
@@ -2486,6 +2486,15 @@ kk_scalarize_filter(const nir_instr *instr, const void *data)
 void
 msl_preprocess_nir(struct nir_shader *nir)
 {
+   /* A function-temp array past this size is spilled to scratch, so its
+    * dynamic index lowers to a flat scratch access rather than an unrolled
+    * branch tree (see the passes below).  A few float4s: under it the tree
+    * is small and the faster form. */
+#define KK_SCRATCH_SPILL_SIZE 64
+   /* Maximum array length lowered to an if-else tree.  Metal's front end is
+    * super-linear in leaf count (see the call site). */
+#define KK_INDIRECT_DEREF_MAX_LEN 16
+
    /* First, inline away all the functions */
    NIR_PASS(_, nir, nir_lower_variable_initializers, nir_var_function_temp);
    NIR_PASS(_, nir, nir_lower_returns);
@@ -2555,9 +2564,33 @@ msl_preprocess_nir(struct nir_shader *nir)
     * dEQP-VK.graphicsfuzz.stable-binarysearch-tree-nested-if-and-conditional */
    NIR_PASS(_, nir, nir_lower_vars_to_scratch, 32,
             glsl_get_natural_size_align_bytes, glsl_get_word_size_align_bytes);
+
+   /* Spill function-temp arrays big enough for an if-else tree to cost real
+    * Metal front-end time, so they take a dynamic index into the "thread"
+    * scratch MSL (a flat access whose build time is constant in the array
+    * length) instead of the tree below.  32 above only spills arrays past
+    * 32 B (a handful of elements), which leaves the big per-light and
+    * per-morph arrays of shader-generated titles to the tree. */
+   NIR_PASS(_, nir, nir_lower_vars_to_scratch, KK_SCRATCH_SPILL_SIZE,
+            glsl_get_natural_size_align_bytes, glsl_get_word_size_align_bytes);
+
+   /* shader_in/out are always lowered in full: nir_to_msl emits them as
+    * load_input/store_output and takes the offset with nir_src_as_uint, so an
+    * indirect index into them cannot be expressed and has to become an
+    * if-else tree here whatever the array length (as before this bound). */
+   NIR_PASS(_, nir, nir_lower_indirect_derefs_to_if_else_trees,
+            nir_var_shader_in | nir_var_shader_out, UINT32_MAX);
+
+   /* Bound the tree for function_temp: an unbounded one (UINT32_MAX) emits a
+    * branch per element and Metal's front end is super-linear in branch
+    * count (a full tree over a large array is tens of seconds of compile on
+    * the presenting thread: the VRChat menu-open / fast-turn freezes).  An
+    * array past the leaf bound stays dynamically indexed, small ones still
+    * tree.  The smaller of the two is the safe direction: MSL crashes on the
+    * 256-leaf case noted above, so a handful of leaves keeps every tree away
+    * from that. */
    NIR_PASS(_, nir, nir_lower_indirect_derefs_to_if_else_trees,
-            nir_var_function_temp | nir_var_shader_in | nir_var_shader_out,
-            UINT32_MAX);
+            nir_var_function_temp, KK_INDIRECT_DEREF_MAX_LEN);
 
    msl_nir_lower_subgroups(nir);
 }
